      "beat_id": "B02ROUNDING",
      "act": "SHOW",
      "heading": "Small numerical changes",
      "narration_text": "Computers store numbers with limited precision, so arithmetic often needs rounding. David Goldberg's classic explanation shows that adding the same numbers in a different order can change the answer. If two token scores are very close, a small numerical change can switch the winner. That new token changes the context for what comes next, so later text can diverge.",
